al media apps  on my phone this was really hard for me  to do because like a lot of you guys  probably I am like totally addicted to  my phone and taking those apps off my  phone really made it abundantly clear  that it's a bit of a problem but I can  only say that this alone probably made  the biggest immediate obvious difference  for me and what I really just come to  realize is that it's just not always so  healthy for me to be constantly checking  up and costly kind of scrolling and  constantly looking at my social media  feeds every hour of the day so that  really really made a difference for me  in my sleep and the last thing that I  did that really helped with my sleeping  was I had to stop with the really strict  sleeping regimes and routines all of  which of course were designed to help  improve my sleep hygiene and help me  sleep better but they were actually  doing the opposite so I felt that I  really had to loosen the reins a bit so  one thing I've been doing is I've been  watching TV in my den with my husband  and I used to never allow myself to  watch TV because again screen time but  one thing I like to do now is I try to  switch up the shows that I watch because  I was finding that I would  memorize the theme song and then when I  hear that theme song come on again even  if my eyes are closer I'm kind of dozing  out I would just kind of like get into  panic mode like oh my god another  episodes gone by I'm not asleep etc so  longer shows our best and kind of boring  shows things that don't require a ton of  concentration so really light-hearted  stuff and I was just finding that  usually I would just fall asleep on the  couch and then I would go upstairs and  and get to bed when I was already in  that like total drowsy state another fun  thing that we've been doing is my  husband and I got like a really long  boring  thousand-piece puzzle oh man puzzles are  so hard so they they're so boring and  sometimes in the middle of the night if  I'm not sleeping that's another thing  that I'll get doing but puzzles are a  great way to kind of just unwind after a  really long day and then some nights  when I'm really already quite tired I  skip the TV downstairs and I skip the  the puzzles or the books or whatever and  I like already just go right into bed  and I'll sometimes just like watch a  little show with my husband on occasion  that happens like maybe once a week and  that is so against the sleep hygiene  rules but I have found that loosening  the rules and being not so rigid in my  sleep routine has actually become the  best way to actually get good sleep  there are definitely days that I still  don't sleep well particularly when you  know I've got something really stressful  going on at work or if I really  overthink the routine but I will say in  general I am doing so much better just  by chilling out a little bit about sleep  I had a therapist once say to me that  the more work we put into trying to  sleep  the harder is to sleep so in other words  sleeping ultimately you should be  thoughtless like it should be effortless  so the same way I talk about intuitive  eating I'm kind of trying to think about  sleep the same way right like sleep and  food and eating are both actually quite  intuitive we're born just knowing and  and wanting these things but it's when  we start to overthink them and  manipulate them that's when they become  over complicated and ultimately that  process gets disturbed so I'm just  trying to think in  those similar terms and put the same  kind of thought process and philosophy  into my sleep that I did employ with my  eating for intuitive eating so guys I  hope you enjoyed this vlog if you did be  sure to give it the thumbs up leave me a  comment below if there's anything else  you guys want me to talk about in my  personal life but also any topics  related to health nutrition etc do you  like these blog videos is there anything  else you'd like to see me do subscribe  to the channel of course and I'll see  you next time on Abby's kitchen bye  [Music]  [Music]
 

